8,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"Match idempotent signatures across BOTH `exc.stderr` and `exc.stdout` (mirroring delete_issue at acli.py:739), not stderr alone, since link delete runs without --json and ACLI may route the 404/409 body to stdout.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"block","decision_margin":0.1,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan: 'narrows to genuine idempotent signatures — stderr matching `404`, `409`, `does not exist`, or `not found` (case-insensitive; absent stderr is NOT idempotent)'","acli.py:739: `err_text = (exc.stderr or \"\") + (exc.stdout or \"\")` then matches '404'/'not found' — the cited sibling checks stdout too","acli_graph.py:644-648: link delete has NO --json, so the CalledProcessError is raised on the exit-code path (acli_subprocess.py:486 `CalledProcessError(returncode, cmd, out, err)`), where a 404/409 body can appear on stdout","AC line: 'A failed `delete_issue_link` with idempotent stderr (404/409/does-not-exist/not-found) still counts applied'"],"finding":"Edit 1 restricts the narrowed idempotent-signature match to stderr only ('stderr matching 404, 409, does not exist, or not found ... absent stderr is NOT idempotent'), but the sibling precedent the plan cites for its shape (delete_issue) matches BOTH streams: `err_text = (exc.stderr or '') + (exc.stdout or '')`. Because `link delete` runs without --json, its CalledProcessError comes from the exit-code path where a 404/409 message may be written to stdout; a stderr-only check would misclassify that idempotent race as a hard failure.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f3ae28ccde3af15f8","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach, edit 1 ('Stop counting failures as applied'); vs acli.py:739 (delete_issue) and acli_graph.py:637-648 (delete_issue_link runs without --json)","norm_id":"na0a9226823a7ad59","priority":0.9,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","scenarios":["Concurrent removal where ACLI writes the 404/409 body to stdout rather than stderr: counted as links_failed=1 and the canary fires under RECONCILER_FAIL_SILENT_NOOP=1 for a benign no-op"],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"In edit 1, compute the idempotency probe over `(exc.stderr or '') + (exc.stdout or '')` (case-insensitive) as delete_issue does, and treat a fully-empty combined text (both streams absent) as NOT idempotent; update the AC and tests to cover a 404 arriving on stdout.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.9,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"no","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"no","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"certification_cannot_prove","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":null,"blocking_enabled":null,"checklist_item":"","cohort":null,"criteria":["P6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":null,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["1 criterion line(s) bundle multiple deliverables with 'and' (split so each is independently verifiable)."],"finding":"Acceptance-criteria / definition-of-done quality issues.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f607dd457c67f9209","impact":0.4,"is_primary":null,"location":"","norm_id":"ned06ebc801a522e3","priority":0.4,"reason":null,"scenarios":[],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"Split compound criteria, replace subjecti